t like we hang out with each  other all the time and it's not like one  monolithic group but we do tend to see  each other from time to time in various  contexts so yeah catch up and  why is it that you all  were friends before like is it just you  happen to all end up at stanford or u of  i or was there some common threat like  what brought you all together because i  think a lot of people look around at  their friend circle like saying college  and they're like man i don't think elon  musk is hanging out here right i don't  think whatever like what brought you all  together what was like the selection  mechanism that you kind of would  attribute uh how you all ended up  together  well so max recruited his um engineering  friends at u of i so i think that was  pretty straightforward and then peter  recruited a number of the people he was  friends with and you know peter had  started had founded the stanford review  which is sort of the conservative  libertarian student newspaper on campus  and i had gone on to become an editor of  that paper several years later so that's  how we met  so there was this libertarian strand to  the founding team and  so  we were all and that was sort of like  this contrarian um  you know  libertarians tend to be not just  contrarian but also sort of um  free market  and so there was a certain sense in  which everybody was cut from  this sort of uh entrepreneurial cloth  now  it's not universally true you know like  uh reed hoffman was not part of the  stanford review in fact he was sort of  on the other extreme he was more liberal  and he still is to this day but he and  peter used to have political debates or  discussions in college and then that's  how reid you know ended up being  recruited by peter so  it's not universally true but there was  something to that that um  the founding team were you know like um  given the sort of the prevailing college  uh the prevailing culture on college  campuses at that time which was sort of  this whole political correctness thing  uh we were rebels against that and i  think that rebel mentality translated  well into becoming founders of  entrepreneurs once we graduated  hey you did you like this video great we  make five of them a day and post them  here on this channel make sure you  subscribe like the video and see you  next time

